  "prompt": "Finance reports 195,532.80 EUR of revenue for store BE-07 in June 2024. These tables may hold errors. BE-07's unit prices in June 2024 were loaded in cents, so the unit_price_eur of every BE-07 order line of June 2024 must be divided by 100, while line_discount_eur is in euros already. A line's revenue is quantity times unit_price_eur minus line_discount_eur. June 2024 means order_ts, as stored, from 1 June 2024 up to but not including 1 July 2024. Return three columns, in this order: revenue_stored, the revenue as stored, and revenue_fixed, the revenue with the prices in euros, both in euros rounded to 2 decimals, then result: 'pass' when revenue_fixed is 195,532.80, otherwise 'fail'. The result is a single row. Any row order is fine.",
